        {
          "Name": "fbTrig",
          "Type": {
            "Class": "R_TRIG"
          },
          "Comment": " Rising edge trigger function block ",
          "Scope": [
            "local"
          ]
        },
        {
          "Name": "xFlip",
          "Type": {
            "Class": "BOOL"
          },
          "Comment": " Internal flip-flop state ",
          "Scope": [
            "local"
          ]
        },
        {
          "Name": "xFlop",
          "Type": {
            "Class": "BOOL"
          },
          "Comment": " Temporary variable for edge detection ",
          "Scope": [
            "temp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "STDeclaration": "FUNCTION_BLOCK FLIP_FLOP\nVAR_INPUT\n\tIN : BOOL; (* Input signal *)\nEND_VAR\nVAR_OUTPUT\n\tQ : BOOL; (* Output signal *)\nEND_VAR\nVAR\n\tfbTrig : R_TRIG; (* Rising edge trigger function block *)\n\txFlip  : BOOL; (* Internal flip-flop state *)\nEND_VAR\nVAR_TEMP\n\txFlop : BOOL; (* Temporary variable for edge detection *)\nEND_VAR\n",
      "STImplementation": "fbTrig(CLK := IN, Q => xFlop);\n\n(* Temporarily disable SA0062 warning. The static analyser incorrectly\n   flags the R_TRIG function block output as always FALSE. It does not\n   have access to the actual run-time behaviour. *)\n{analysis -62}\nIF xFlop {analysis +62} THEN\n\txFlip := NOT xFlip;\nEND_IF\n\n(* Use a temporary variable for edge detection in order to avoid reading\n   the previous state from the output. *)\nQ := xFlip;\n"
    },
    "PT1": {
      "Name": "PT1",
      "ObjectType": "FunctionBlock",
      "Verbatim": "FUNCTION_BLOCK PT1",
      "Variables": [
        {
          "Name": "IN",
          "Type": {
            "Class": "REAL"
          },
          "Comment": " Input signal ",
          "Scope": [
            "input"
          ]
        },
        {
          "Name": "P",
          "Type": {
            "Class": "REAL"
          },
          "Comment": " Proportional factor ",
          "Initial": "0.2",
          "Scope": [
            "input"
          ]
        },
        {
          "Name": "Q",
          "Type": {
            "Class": "REAL"
          },
          "Comment": " Output signal ",
          "Scope": [
            "output"
          ]
        },
        {
          "Name": "Q1",
          "Type": {
            "Class": "REAL"
          },
          "Comment": " Previous output signal, used for feedback ",
          "Scope": [
            "local"
          ]
        },
        {
          "Name": "P1",
          "Type": {
            "Class": "REAL"
          },
          "Comment": " Limited proportional factor ",
          "Scope": [
            "temp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "STDeclaration": "FUNCTION_BLOCK PT1\nVAR_INPUT\n\tIN : REAL;        (* Input signal *)\n\tP  : REAL := 0.2; (* Proportional factor *)\nEND_VAR\nVAR_OUTPUT\n\tQ : REAL; (* Output signal *)\nEND_VAR\nVAR\n\tQ1 : REAL; (* Previous output signal, used for feedback *)\nEND_VAR\nVAR_TEMP\n\tP1 : REAL; (* Limited proportional factor *)\nEND_VAR\n",
      "STImplementation": "(* First, limit the proportional factor to the range [0, 1] because\nvalues outside this range could lead to instability or unexpected\nbehaviour. Next, calculate the output signal using the limited\nproportional factor and the internal state, i.e. the previous output\nsignal. The current cycle's output becomes the next cycle's feedback. *)\nP1 := LIMIT(0, P, 1);\nQ1 := (IN * P1) + (Q1 * (1 - P1));\nQ  := Q1;\n"
    },
